{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775333451-NlbOxJinnCEpFLyLRnXi","role":"assistant","created":1775333459,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I don't see any unemployment data in the resources. The task asks me to use the monthly U.S. unemployment rate for calendar year 1961 from the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics. Let me search online or use known historical data for 1961.\n\nActually, I should first extract the Treasury data properly from the files. Let me extract the monthly average balance data for 1961 from the Treasury Bulletin. I have the data from the page 35 of the 1961 December bulletin:\n\nFrom the table in treasury_bulletin_1961_12_page_35.txt:\n- 1961-January: Average = 3,414\n- February: Average = 3,812\n- March: Average = 3,705\n- April: Average = 2,171\n- May: Average = 3,765\n- June: Average = 3,572\n- July: Average = 3,739\n- August: Average = 4,581\n- September: Average = 4,277\n- October: Average = 5,924\n- November: Average = 4,873\n- And from treasury_bulletin_1962_12_page_44.txt:\n- 1961-December: Average = 3,869\n\nSo for 1961, the monthly average balance (in millions of dollars) is:\n- Jan: 3414\n- Feb: 3812\n- Mar: 3705\n- Apr: 2171\n- May: 3765\n- Jun: 3572\n- Jul: 3739\n- Aug: 4581\n- Sep: 4277\n- Oct: 5924\n- Nov: 4873\n- Dec: 3869\n\nNow I need the unemployment rate data for 1961. Let me try to find this data from a web search or known historical data.\n\nActually, since it's not in the resources, I need to look it up. Let me use curl or wget to access BLS data, or I could look for it online.\n\n\nI can retrieve the unemployment data directly from the BLS website using the series ID for the unemployment rate.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_061dd1659e82465ab787b358","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://data.bls.gov/timeseries/LNS14000000\" 2>/dev/null | head -100"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
